course: dictionary
lesson: 9518
title: Stiffness: hard to bend, or tight and awkward
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Stiffness is a noun, from the word stiff. It can mean something is hard to bend, like a new board, or a tight, achy feeling in your body after exercise or a bad night's sleep. Read the words around it to find which meaning fits.
explain: «One doctor cracked the knuckles of one hand for 60 years and found no arthritis, a painful stiffness of the joints.» The joints are where bones meet, so stiffness here means a tight, achy feeling in the joints. Check it: swap in "tight, achy feeling" and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Stiffness can also describe how a person acts. Stiffness in manners means someone is too formal, cold or awkward. Science uses the word too: engineers test the stiffness of beams and springs, which means how strongly they resist bending or stretching.
fact: Stiffness is an uncountable noun, so say some stiffness, not a stiffness.
fact: Stiffness in the body is a tight, achy feeling in your muscles or joints.
fact: Morning stiffness is the tight feeling you can get when you first wake up.
fact: Stiffness in how someone acts means being too formal, cold or awkward, not relaxed.
fact: In science, stiffness is how strongly a material resists being bent or stretched.
exercise: «One doctor cracked the knuckles of one hand for 60 years and found no arthritis, a painful stiffness of the joints.» What does stiffness mean here? | Being very fast at running | A sweet smell from the kitchen | *A tight, achy feeling in the joints | A loud crack like a pop
exercise: Mia says the new ruler has stiffness because it will not bend. What does stiffness mean here? | How much it weighs | How quickly it can run | *How hard something is to bend | How loud it is when dropped
exercise: A character answers with stiffness, very formal and cold, and does not smile. What does stiffness suggest? | *Being formal, cold or awkward | Being very cheerful | Being very tired and sleepy | Being loud and noisy
test: Which word is the noun for "stiff"? | stiffen | stiffly | *stiffness | stiff
test: After sleeping badly, Sam wakes with a tight, achy neck. What is this? | *A sign of stiffness in the body | Stiffness in how someone acts | Stiffness of a spring | A bad dream
exam: Which sentence uses stiffness in the science sense? | The stiffness of the room made the children giggle | Her stiffness made everyone at the party feel uneasy | *Engineers tested the stiffness of the steel beam to see how much it bent | His morning stiffness went away after a warm bath
